.TH SDL_GetCameraSupportedFormats 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetCameraSupportedFormats \- Get the list of native formats/sizes a camera supports.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_camera.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_CameraSpec ** SDL_GetCameraSupportedFormats(SDL_CameraID instance_id, int *count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This returns a list of all formats and frame sizes that a specific camera can offer\[char46] This is useful if your app can accept a variety of image formats and sizes and so want to find the optimal spec that doesn\(aqt require conversion\[char46]
.PP
This function isn\(aqt strictly required; if you call
.BR SDL_OpenCamera
with a NULL spec, SDL will choose a native format for you, and if you instead specify a desired format, it will transparently convert to the requested format on your behalf\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR count
is not NULL, it will be filled with the number of elements in the returned array\[char46]
.PP
Note that it\(aqs legal for a camera to supply an empty list\[char46] This is what will happen on Emscripten builds, since that platform won\(aqt tell _anything_ about available cameras until you\(aqve opened one, and won\(aqt even tell if there _is_ a camera until the user has given you permission to check through a scary warning popup\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I instance_id
the camera device instance ID\[char46]
.TP
.I count
a pointer filled in with the number of elements in the list, may be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a NULL terminated array of pointers to
.BR SDL_CameraSpec
or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46] This is a single allocation that should be freed with
.BR SDL_free ()
when it is no longer needed\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetCameras (3),
